current_companion_truth:
  contract: loopback-capability/4 + acquire.v2 + operation.v3 + operation-projection.v2
  source: exact pinned Qwen/Qwen3-0.6B revision c1899de289a04d12100db370d81485cdf75e47ca
  source_lock: contracts/vnext/qwen3-0.6b-base-source-lock.v2.json; sha256:50a8c29e36398a9a088e4d9a224dad186809d34b1e050299d3ce3de7a01b7d0e; descriptor /2 corrects the pinned upstream license identity. Historical source lock v1 is not admitted by current acquisition.
  result: Production bounded source acquisition, exclusive operation ownership, contained converter launch, terminal reconciliation, independent six-member inspection/transfer, and listener wiring are implemented.
  blocker: No authorized real-source acquisition receipt through this coordinator or qualified real model is established by current implementation and fixture evidence. Available and local seed readiness are not qualification or outside-network proof.
  browser: Current worktree product UI loads the capability client, composition installer, and qualified direct-P2P acquisition path; this is source wiring, not real-model browser or deployment proof.
  source_eligibility: The unchanged pinned Qwen3-0.6B remains rejected as a product model and is diagnostic ancestry only; a later derivative needs genuinely different bytes and independent untouched qualification.
  numerical: Native and browser WASM share the scalar runtime. Historical composition /12 is structural-only; numerical execution v2 closed with source-trace-environment-drift, not parity. The current profile binds the prepared /3 owner and helpers with environment-lock.v2 and the corrected source lock. A real v3 registration and material gates remain required; the ancestry stays rejected for product use.
  numerical_reference: artifacts/external/qwen3-numerical-oracle/environment/Scripts/python.exe; actual environment admission and pinned synthetic framework tests pass. Installer cleanup is policy-blocked, and two dangling temporary links currently prevent the source-authority scan from completing. See ecosystem experiment lesson C28 and the owner-run numerical-installer cleanup.
  numerical_launch_boundary: C29 requires canonical source/artifact/model locations, source-authority preflight, minimal child/termination environments and isolated Python flags. All 56 affected checks pass; Node coverage inheritance caused three initial failures and now has explicit suppression. See numerical-execution-boundary-review.json and experiment lesson C29. Closed v2 metadata still cannot authorize a new run.
  next_gate: Finish source/release checks and a fresh v3 diagnostic registration; establish an eligible exact product checkpoint and obtain real native/WASM, quality, browser, and P2P evidence. Never replay or adopt closed failed operations, including /10. C30 removes active v2 compatibility; all 58 affected checks pass with no model or publication claim.
  routing_boundary: These source-state pointers correct obsolete owner-missing and browser-unloaded guidance; earlier checkpoint hashes, test counts, wiki records, and terminal decisions remain historical and immutable.
